weightedConnectedComponents -- Counting the weighted number of connected components of a graph
**********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        weightedConnectedComponents(G)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a Graph or a List
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * WeightMethod (missing documentation) => ..., default value "PBEI", 
  * Outputs:
      * the (weighted) number of connected components of G

Description
===========

This computes the (weighted) number of connected components of a graph. The
weights are all one if WeightMethod='BEI' is chosen and if WeightMethod='PBEI',
then bipartite components count twice.
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G={{1,2},{2,3},{3,1},{4,5},{6,7},{7,8},{6,8}};     |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : weightedConnectedComponents(G,WeightMethod=>"BEI") |
|                                                        |
|o2 = 3                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : weightedConnectedComponents(G,WeightMethod=>"PBEI")|
|                                                        |
|o3 = 4                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note disconnectors: disconnectors, -- Disconnectors of a graph

